    {
      "head": "7f85b137835907b3a786dec225a49e9ff694537a",
      "subject": "osctld: report bounded pool storage activity",
      "message": "osctld: report bounded pool storage activity\n\nTrack per-pool garbage collector and trash work from enqueue through\ncompletion, including timer prunes and synchronous moves. Report a\nread-only, versioned pool sample with stable daemon and import identities,\na monotonic generation, worker status, and sticky unknown conditions.\n\nKeep absent or stopping pools unknown. Add unit and VM command coverage\nwithout changing GC stop behavior or granting repair authority.",
      "paths": [
        "docs/osctld/interfaces.md",
        "osctld/lib/osctld/commands/pool/export.rb",
        "osctld/lib/osctld/commands/pool/storage_activity.rb",
        "osctld/lib/osctld/daemon.rb",
        "osctld/lib/osctld/garbage_collector.rb",
        "osctld/lib/osctld/pool.rb",
        "osctld/lib/osctld/storage_activity.rb",
        "osctld/lib/osctld/trash_bin.rb",
        "osctld/spec/osctld/commands/heavy_system_spec.rb",
        "osctld/spec/osctld/commands/simple_delegators_spec.rb",
        "osctld/spec/osctld/garbage_collector_spec.rb",
        "osctld/spec/osctld/storage_activity_spec.rb",
        "osctld/spec/osctld/trash_bin_spec.rb",
        "tests/all-tests.nix",
        "tests/suite/osctld/storage-activity.nix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "head": "09786fbc20a2d8e134e2e3001d53ef287646e74b",
      "subject": "os: support generations without automatic osctld startup",
      "message": "os: support generations without automatic osctld startup\n\nAdd osctld.enable with the existing enabled behavior as its default.\nDisabled generations retain the service, configuration and tools while\nrefusing declarative pools, exportfs, pool installation and\ncontradictory runlevel membership.\n\nKeep raw ZFS import, mounts and properties available without waiting for\nosctld or associating pools with it. Configuration activation consults\nits parsed destination runlevel before invoking osctl and keeps the\nexisting restart handling for selected services.\n\nCover actual module outputs and activation classes in a focused check.\nExtend the existing switch scenario to preserve dataset identity and a\nknown payload across activation, a fresh disabled boot and return to\nordinary startup using the same framework machine and retained disks.\n\nThis changes no retained format and grants no physical exclusion or\nmaintenance authority. Older ordinary generations can restart writers;\nbooting one is not a safe rollback while storage maintenance is owned.",
      "paths": [
        "docs/os/runlevels.md",
        "flake.nix",
        "os/modules/osctl/osctld.nix",
        "os/modules/system/activation/switch-to-configuration.rb",
        "os/modules/tasks/filesystems/zfs/pool-service.nix",
        "tests/osctld-disabled-eval.nix",
        "tests/suite/system/switch-to-configuration.nix"
      ]
    }
  ],
